-- title:
--   Height-one section prime for an admissible crossing value at j=0
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$, and assume $0 \in$ `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $0$ has trivial $q$-torsion in its affine point group. Let $K \subset \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be a number field, put $A_K = A \cap K$ = `coeffSubring A K`, and let $\varpi \in A_K$ be such that an element of $A_K$ reduces to $0$ under the restricted reduction if and only if it is a multiple of $\varpi$; let $e_K \ge 1$ and a unit $\varepsilon$ satisfy $q = \varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$ in $A_K$. Write $R_0$ for `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A_K … 0 (0 ^ q)`, the ring of Laurent series $f$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for which $f \cdot s(j_{\mathsf q}, j_{\mathsf q, q}) = r(j_{\mathsf q}, j_{\mathsf q, q})$ for some two-variable polynomials $r, s$ over $A_K$ with $s$ not vanishing at the reduced point $(0, 0^q)$, and let $\tilde\varpi \in R_0$ be the constant series $\varpi$. The hypotheses on $R_0$ are a crossing presentation at the node: elements $G', H', w \in R_0$ with $w$ a unit and $G'H' = \tilde\varpi^{\,\mathrm{jWidth}(0)\cdot e_K} w$, where $\mathrm{jWidth}(0) = 3$; the maximal ideal of $R_0$ (for any local-ring structure on it) is $(\tilde\varpi, G', H')$; the ideals $(\tilde\varpi, G')$ and $(\tilde\varpi, H')$ are prime, with $H' \notin (\tilde\varpi, G')$ and $G' \notin (\tilde\varpi, H')$, and they coincide with $(\tilde\varpi, j_{\mathsf q,q} - j_{\mathsf q}^{\,q})$ and $(\tilde\varpi, j_{\mathsf q} - j_{\mathsf q,q}^{\,q})$ respectively. Finally let $c$ lie in the maximal ideal of $A$ and be admissible, i.e. $cm = q^3$ for some $m$ in that maximal ideal, and let $K' \supseteq K$ be a number field containing $c$. The conclusion is twofold: the series $G'$ lies in `fieldOver (1 * q) K'`, the subfield of Laurent series generated by the constants from $K'$ together with $j_{\mathsf q}$ and $j_{\mathsf q, q}$; and the ring $C' =$ `jIntegralClosure (1 * q) A K'` of elements of that subfield integral over the subring generated by the constants from $A \cap K'$ and $j_{\mathsf q}$ carries a prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ of height $1$ with $q \notin \mathfrak p$ such that, for every two-variable polynomial $s$ over $A \cap K'$ not vanishing at the reduced point $(0, 0^q)$, the element $s(j_{\mathsf q}, j_{\mathsf q, q})$ lies outside $\mathfrak p$ whenever it lies in $C'$, and there are $r_0, r, s \in C'$ with $s \notin \mathfrak p$, $r \in \mathfrak p$, $G' s = r_0$, $(G' - c)s = r$, $r \ne 0$, and every $t \in \mathfrak p$ satisfying $tv = ru$ for some $u, v \in C'$ with $v \notin \mathfrak p$.
--
--   This is the algebraisation of the section $u = c$ of the tube around the supersingular node $j = 0$, of width three in the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(q)$: from a crossing presentation of the node ring it produces a height-one prime of the normal model over a larger number field at which $G'$ takes the admissible value $c$, together with the local generation of that prime by $G' - c$. It is used in the construction of the place centred at the node with prescribed value and in the computation of the order of vanishing of $G' - c$ there.
